WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
Ok, let’s make a gazpacho

00:01.000 --> 00:04.000
classic style, but in a super quick version.

00:04.000 --> 00:07.000
Listen up. A fresh and authentic dish

00:07.000 --> 00:08.000
ready in no time? Yes,

00:08.000 --> 00:11.000
it is possible. First, the main players.

00:11.000 --> 00:13.000
These are the ingredients that will

00:13.000 --> 00:16.000
bring everything to life: tomato, cucumber,

00:16.000 --> 00:18.000
pepper, garlic and bread. This is the base.

00:18.000 --> 00:21.000
With this, you just can’t go wrong. Really ripe

00:21.000 --> 00:23.000
tomatoes, half a cucumber, one pepper and

00:23.000 --> 00:26.000
a touch of garlic, or just half a clove so it’s not too strong.

00:26.000 --> 00:28.000
To give it body, a bit of day‑old bread.

00:28.000 --> 00:30.000
Around 50 to 100 grams

00:30.000 --> 00:33.000
is perfect. Now, the liquid gold: three or

00:33.000 --> 00:35.000
four tablespoons of good extra

00:35.000 --> 00:37.000
virgin olive oil. And the acidic

00:37.000 --> 00:39.000
kick, super important: one tablespoon

00:39.000 --> 00:42.000
of sherry vinegar, that special touch. And to

00:42.000 --> 00:44.000
finish, a glass of very cold water

00:44.000 --> 00:46.000
to lighten it up and, of course, salt

00:46.000 --> 00:48.000
to taste. Time for action.

00:48.000 --> 00:50.000
The preparation is super simple, just three

00:50.000 --> 00:53.000
quick steps. Chop everything up,

00:53.000 --> 00:55.000
add the liquids and the salt and

00:55.000 --> 00:58.000
blend on high speed. Now for the final touch.

00:58.000 --> 01:00.000
This is where you choose the style

01:00.000 --> 01:01.000
of your gazpacho.

01:01.000 --> 01:03.000
You have to decide: do you like it

01:03.000 --> 01:05.000
rustic, unstrained, or smoother,

01:05.000 --> 01:08.000
passing it through a strainer? And here’s

01:08.000 --> 01:10.000
the big secret: let it chill really well

01:10.000 --> 01:13.000
in the fridge. It has to be very cold. And once

01:13.000 --> 01:15.000
everything is ready, the best moment comes:

01:15.000 --> 01:18.000
serving and enjoying. You can serve it in a glass,

01:18.000 --> 01:20.000
which looks super tempting, or in a more

01:20.000 --> 01:23.000
traditional bowl. And on top, what works best?

01:23.000 --> 01:25.000
Some crunchy croutons or

01:25.000 --> 01:27.000
finely chopped fresh veggies.
